1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,744
Look! I'm walking with the sheep!

2
00:00:04,144 --> 00:00:08,243
The sun is going down... It's so beautiful!

3
00:00:08,693 --> 00:00:16,363
I'm walking with the sheep. The sun is going down. Mia is describing what is happening right now. This is the present continuous.

4
00:00:16,963 --> 00:00:21,835
In this lesson, you'll learn how to make it, when to use it, and when not to use it.

5
00:00:22,785 --> 00:00:26,534
We use the present continuous for actions in progress.

6
00:00:27,134 --> 00:00:31,029
Right now, at this moment: she's reading a map right now.

7
00:00:31,629 --> 00:00:35,371
Around now, these days: I'm learning English this year.

8
00:00:35,971 --> 00:00:40,155
Temporary situations: he's staying with his grandma this week.

9
00:00:40,755 --> 00:00:45,688
And fixed future plans, with a time: we're meeting Ali tomorrow at five.

10
00:00:46,288 --> 00:00:50,270
In all of them, the action is not finished. It's in progress.

11
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:56,425
Look at Mia. She's walking through the grass. The wind is blowing, and the sheep are eating.

12
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:03,045
The form has two parts: am, is or are, plus the verb with i n g.

13
00:01:03,645 --> 00:01:06,912
I am walking. In speaking: I'm walking.

14
00:01:07,512 --> 00:01:10,058
She is walking. She's walking.

15
00:01:10,658 --> 00:01:13,153
They are walking. They're walking.

16
00:01:13,753 --> 00:01:17,477
Both parts are important. Don't forget am, is or are!

17
00:01:18,427 --> 00:01:22,534
Spelling. Most verbs just add i n g: read, reading.

18
00:01:23,134 --> 00:01:28,243
If the verb ends in a silent e, drop the e: make, making. Write, writing.

19
00:01:28,843 --> 00:01:35,836
One short vowel and one consonant at the end? Double the consonant: run, running. Sit, sitting. Swim, swimming.

20
00:01:36,436 --> 00:01:40,087
And i e becomes y: lie, lying. Die, dying.

21
00:01:40,687 --> 00:01:45,085
But be careful: see, seeing. Play, playing. These just add i n g.

22
00:01:46,185 --> 00:01:52,246
Oh no! Whiskers is jumping across the river. Mia is reaching out her hand. Is he going to make it?

23
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:56,637
For the negative, add not after am, is or are.

24
00:01:57,237 --> 00:01:59,003
I'm not sleeping.

25
00:01:59,603 --> 00:02:01,199
She isn't listening.

26
00:02:01,799 --> 00:02:03,523
They aren't playing now.

27
00:02:04,123 --> 00:02:07,827
Remember: we say I'm not. There is no amn't in English.

28
00:02:08,727 --> 00:02:13,128
I'm not sleeping. I'm watching the sunset!

29
00:02:13,578 --> 00:02:16,722
For questions, put am, is or are first.

30
00:02:17,322 --> 00:02:20,613
Are you listening? Yes, I am. Or, no, I'm not.

31
00:02:21,213 --> 00:02:23,748
Is it raining? No, it isn't.

32
00:02:24,348 --> 00:02:26,902
What are you doing? I'm reading a map.

33
00:02:27,502 --> 00:02:30,251
Where is she going? She's going home.

34
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:34,325
What are you doing, Whiskers?

35
00:02:34,775 --> 00:02:38,163
Some words often go with the present continuous.

36
00:02:38,763 --> 00:02:41,234
Now. Right now. At the moment.

37
00:02:41,834 --> 00:02:44,431
Today. This week. These days.

38
00:02:45,031 --> 00:02:51,146
And look and listen, when we point at something happening: look! It's snowing. Listen! The baby is crying.

39
00:02:52,096 --> 00:02:55,136
How is it different from the present simple?

40
00:02:55,736 --> 00:03:02,936
The present simple is for habits: she walks to school every day. The continuous is for now: she's walking to school now.

41
00:03:03,536 --> 00:03:07,456
I usually drink tea. But today, I'm drinking coffee.

42
00:03:08,056 --> 00:03:13,228
He works in a bank, that's permanent. But he's working from home this week, that's temporary.

43
00:03:14,178 --> 00:03:19,550
Some verbs describe states, not actions. We don't usually use them with i n g.

44
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:22,270
Like, love, want, need.

45
00:03:22,870 --> 00:03:25,292
Know, understand, believe.

46
00:03:25,892 --> 00:03:32,928
And have, when it means own. So: I understand, not I'm understanding. I want ice cream, not I'm wanting ice cream.

47
00:03:33,878 --> 00:03:36,050
The most common mistakes.

48
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:40,072
I reading now. We need am: I'm reading now.

49
00:03:40,672 --> 00:03:44,905
She is play football. Add i n g: she is playing football.

50
00:03:45,505 --> 00:03:50,196
I am understanding you. Understand is a state verb: I understand you.

51
00:03:50,796 --> 00:03:53,482
Are you go home? Are you going home?

52
00:03:54,082 --> 00:03:57,626
He is siting there. Double the t: he is sitting there.

53
00:03:58,576 --> 00:04:01,924
Now say them with me. Listen, then repeat.

54
00:04:02,824 --> 00:04:04,633
I'm learning English.

55
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:09,806
She's reading a book right now.

56
00:04:12,906 --> 00:04:14,433
They aren't playing.

57
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:18,535
What are you doing?

58
00:04:21,235 --> 00:04:23,089
Look! It's raining.

59
00:04:25,839 --> 00:04:30,306
Let's watch a little story. What's happening? Listen for i n g.

60
00:04:31,406 --> 00:04:38,735
Mia is crossing the river. The water is rushing over the stones. She's holding a long stick, and she's walking very slowly.

61
00:04:39,835 --> 00:04:45,440
Now she's on the other side. Whiskers is purring, and Mia is smiling. They're hugging each other.

62
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:50,438
The sun is going down... It's so beautiful!

63
00:04:50,888 --> 00:04:54,511
Quiz time! Five questions, five seconds each.

64
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:58,707
Number 1. Shh! The baby blank.

65
00:05:04,507 --> 00:05:07,347
Is sleeping. It's happening right now.

66
00:05:08,247 --> 00:05:11,290
Number 2. They blank football at the moment.

67
00:05:17,090 --> 00:05:18,888
Are playing. They are.

68
00:05:19,788 --> 00:05:22,656
Number 3. Look! He's blank in the sea.

69
00:05:28,456 --> 00:05:30,680
Swimming, with double m.

70
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:34,258
Number 4. I blank the answer.

71
00:05:40,058 --> 00:05:43,379
Know. Know is a state verb, so no i n g.

72
00:05:44,279 --> 00:05:47,150
Number 5. blank you listening to me?

73
00:05:52,950 --> 00:05:55,154
Are. Are you listening to me?

74
00:05:56,054 --> 00:06:04,325
Let's remember. The present continuous is for actions in progress, now or around now, for temporary situations, and for fixed plans.

75
00:06:04,925 --> 00:06:12,501
It's am, is or are, plus verb i n g, with careful spelling. Negatives with not, and questions with am, is or are first.

76
00:06:13,101 --> 00:06:17,085
And no i n g with state verbs like know, like and want.

77
00:06:18,035 --> 00:06:23,556
Your homework: look around you, and write five things that are happening right now, in the comments.

78
00:06:24,156 --> 00:06:28,147
Subscribe for more lessons. See you in the next one. Bye!

